{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Out of the midst of the fire, the cloud, and the darkness</b> — an explanation of <b>out of the midst of the fire</b>, for cloud and darkness are around Him." "<b>A great voice, and it did not cease</b>. They translate it [in Onkelos]: וְלֹא פְּסַק — and it did not cease, for the nature of flesh and blood is that they cannot speak their words in a single breath, but the nature of the Holy One, blessed be He, is not so — He did not cease, and since He did not cease, He did not add [more], for His voice is strong and enduring forever. Alternatively, לֹא יָסַף — He did not again show Himself publicly in that manner; this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Deuteronomy 5:19).\n\nNow, Scripture says (Exodus 19:19), 'And the voice of the shofar grew louder and louder,' and they said (Mekhilta Yitro 4): Why was it soft at first? To accustom the ear to what it could hear. But perhaps this was so with the voice of the shofar, whereas the voice of HaShem in the Ten Commandments was uniform throughout.\n\nThe correct interpretation is that the one who says לֹא פָּסַק derives יָסַף from 'וְנֶאֶסְפָה שִׂמְחָה וָגִיל' (Jeremiah 48:33), 'תּוֹסִיף רוּחָם יִגְוָעוּן' (Psalms 104:29) — whose meaning, in his view, is the withholding of a thing — so he says that His greatness and power were not withheld until He completed all the commandments. Similarly it says, 'וַיִּתְנַבְּאוּ וְלֹא יָסְפוּ' (Numbers 11:25).\n\nAccording to the plain sense, וְלֹא יָסַף means it did not increase to be any greater than it was.\n\nAnd by way of truth, one says that all these things — they heard a great voice, וְלֹא יָסַף — He did not add to make heard to your entire assembly anything but a single voice, for that voice alone is what they attained. I have already explained this matter there (Exodus 20) and in the entire passage."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {1 "The verse reference Exodus 19:20 in the last line appears corrupt; the discussion concerns the revelation at Sinai (Exodus 19–20), translated hyper-literally as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:45:53.015009430Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}